      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is double the usual maximum:\n- The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- Single doses are usually capped at 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg PO twice daily**, which is the standard range.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm the dose and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
